course: dictionary
lesson: 8189
title: A place to eat out
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A restaurant is a place where people pay to sit down and eat a meal that is cooked and served there. You do not cook it yourself. Look at the clues in the words around it: pay, sit and served all tell you what a restaurant is for.
explain: «In a restaurant you speak quietly, stay in your seat and are polite to the waiter.» These clues tell you how to behave there: quiet voices, sitting still and good manners. A restaurant is not a playground.
explain: «A boy in Sydney ran through a busy restaurant and crashed into a waiter carrying hot soup; the soup spilled on his arm and burned him.» Running is dangerous there, because waiters carry hot food and drinks past the tables.
fact: A restaurant is a place where people pay to sit and eat meals that are cooked and served there.
fact: «De l'eau plate» is still water, and «de l'eau gazeuse» is sparkling water.
fact: In French restaurants, «une carafe d'eau» is tap water, and it is free.
fact: In a sit-down restaurant in the USA, people usually leave a tip of about 15 to 20 percent, so on a $40 bill that is about $6 to $8.
fact: Phrases to know: go to a restaurant, eat at a restaurant, Italian restaurant, restaurant bill.
exercise: What is a restaurant? | A shop that sells clothes | *A place where people pay to sit and eat meals cooked and served there | A school for cooks | A park with swings and a slide
exercise: «A boy in Sydney ran through a busy restaurant and crashed into a waiter carrying hot soup.» What should he have done instead? | Jumped on the tables | Run faster to win | *Walked carefully and stayed safe | Shouted to his friends
exercise: Sam is eating in a sit-down restaurant in the USA. The bill is $40. About how much tip is usual? | About $60 to $80 | *About $6 to $8 | About $40 exactly | About $1
test: What does «de l'eau plate» mean? | *Still water | Sparkling water | Tap water | Hot soup
test: In a restaurant, how should you behave? | Lie on the floor | *Speak quietly, stay in your seat and be polite | Speak loudly and wander around | Run and shout with your friends
exam: Which sentence best describes a restaurant? | People cook their own food at home | A place where people go swimming | A place to buy clothes and shoes | *People pay to sit and eat meals that are cooked and served there
